{"summary": "I implemented `transpose` in `transpose.py`, and it gives the expected output for the examples I tried.

It splits the input into lines. Each line gets spaces added on its right only as far as the longest line below it, so short lines above long ones come out padded on the left, and nothing is padded on the right. Spaces that are already in the input are kept. Then it reads the columns off as the output rows. Empty input returns `""`.

I checked it by hand with `python -c`, since the project has no test files. The two uneven examples from the instructions, empty input, and a staircase-shaped input all matched what I expected. I haven't run it against the hidden tests."}
